Tesla landed an $800 million megapack deal with zero for three gigawatt hours of storage capacity in Italy. This is Tesla Shorts Time, episode 602. Zero signed an agreement for three gigawatt hours of megapack capacity valued at approximately $800 million. The project targets utility scale storage deployment across Italy. The deal represents one of Tesla Energy's larger international orders to date.

00:00:27.620 --> 00:00:56.920
Megapack units will be installed to support grid stability and renewable integration. The same battery technology now appears in customer vehicles through a new cyber truck function. The update enables the cyber truck to supply electricity to a home during outages. It builds on existing power share hardware already in the vehicle. Owners can now draw from the trucks battery pack when grid power is down. The feature it integrates directly with the vehicle's existing electrical architecture.

00:00:56.920 --> 00:01:12.460
Tesla also recorded its busiest delivery day of the quarter in Norway, moving 171 vehicles in a single day. The surge came primarily from model Y variants. The daily figure stands out against typical delivery patterns in the market.

00:01:12.460 --> 00:01:31.380
Norway remains one of Tesla's stronger European markets for volume. In Los Angeles, EVGO opened its largest non-Tesla charging station in the area. The new station includes Chadamo connectors for older Nissan leaf vehicles. It adds significant capacity for drivers outside the Tesla ecosystem.

00:01:31.380 --> 00:01:50.720
EVGO continues to expand its network with legacy connector support. The latest supervised FSD version can intervene automatically to avoid collisions. The system takes control without driver input in certain detected scenarios. The feature activates when the software identifies an imminent impact risk.

00:01:50.720 --> 00:02:09.960
Tesla continues to refine the supervised FSD stack with additional safety interventions. Supervised FSD executed a reverse maneuver to allow a bus to pass at a tight intersection. The behavior occurred without driver intervention. The system assessed the space constraints and backed up to create clearance.

00:02:09.960 --> 00:02:28.340
Tesla has been testing edge case handling in complex urban environments. A dedicated Robotaxi service area is planned at the Wesley Chapel location in Florida. The addition supports local testing and fleet operations. The service center will handle charging and maintenance for the driverless vehicles.

00:02:28.340 --> 00:02:45.760
Tesla is expanding its Robotaxi footprint through existing service locations. The cyber cab was displayed without steering wheel or pedals during its Japan debut. No domestic launch timeline has been confirmed. The vehicle was shown as a fully autonomous taxi concept.

00:02:45.760 --> 00:02:56.040
Tesla indicated interest in future market expansion but left the schedule open. Rising diesel costs improve the total cost of ownership case for the Tesla semi.

00:02:56.720 --> 00:03:07.120
Fleet's already operating the truck report lower per mile energy expenses. The article notes that sustained high fuel prices widen the operating cost gap versus diesel rigs.

00:03:07.120 --> 00:03:23.140
Tesla's semi program continues to target long haul routes where energy savings matter most owners of pre 2021 model S and model X vehicles will receive a significant software refresh. The changes target infotainment and connectivity features.

00:03:23.700 --> 00:03:33.520
Tesla is delivering the update to cars that predate the current refreshed versions of those models. The refresh focuses on bringing newer interface elements to the older hardware.

00:03:33.520 --> 00:03:48.120
The browser in software version 2026.32 now includes an ad blocking feature owners report cleaner web browsing inside the vehicle. The change removes advertisements from web pages viewed on the car's screen.

00:03:48.860 --> 00:04:00.420
Tesla rolled out the update as part of the broader 2026.32 software branch. The boring company raised $3 billion in around that values the tunneling firm at $23 billion.

00:04:01.420 --> 00:04:10.080
Funds will support expanded tunnel networks designed for Tesla vehicle use. The investment round was led by investors focused on infrastructure projects.

00:04:10.720 --> 00:04:19.920
The boring company's tunnels are intended to carry Tesla vehicles in urban settings. BYD maintained a sizable lead in quarterly EV deliveries over Tesla.

00:04:19.920 --> 00:04:36.260
The gap has persisted across multiple quarters despite Tesla's new model launches. Tesla's production ramp outside China remains the main variable in narrowing the difference. BYD captured 35.4% of Chinese EV exports in the latest period.

00:04:36.740 --> 00:04:45.180
The company outpaced Tesla and overseas shipments from its home market. The gap highlights shifting global supply dynamics for battery electric vehicles.

00:04:45.180 --> 00:04:55.960
Volkswagen led EV sales growth outside China while Tesla placed second in the ranking. The data covers multiple international markets beyond the Chinese domestic segment.

00:04:56.600 --> 00:05:08.060
Tesla maintained a strong position even as competition intensified. Factory output numbers draw the most attention yet the real constraint on scaling often sits one layer deeper in component yield.

00:05:08.060 --> 00:05:18.460
When a battery cell line must hit both energy density targets and cost per kilowatt hour goals simultaneously, any shortfall in one forces a trade off in the other.

00:05:19.100 --> 00:05:30.820
Tesla's 4680 program has published incremental gains in both metrics but the published data still show cell level yield as the variable that directly multiplies or divides total pack output.

00:05:30.820 --> 00:05:45.120
That same yield problem appears in a different form at the vehicle assembly level where a structural battery pack that also serves as the chassis floor reduces part count yet transfers the burden of dimensional precision onto the cell supplier.

00:05:45.580 --> 00:05:53.640
If a single cell batch falls outside tolerance, the entire pack may be rejected rather than reworked, raising the effective scrap rate.

00:05:53.640 --> 00:06:01.460
Rivals that keep cells in separate modules can isolate defects more easily, though they carry higher assembly labor and weight.

00:06:02.020 --> 00:06:12.800
The business consequence is straightforward because every percentage point of improvement in cell yield lowers the capital required per delivered vehicle and per installed megawatt hour of storage.

00:06:13.800 --> 00:06:19.800
